BIG terrain perf win (the foliage-prewarm + physics-heightfield bottleneck): the mapspinner CPU height sampler (height-cpu groundHeightLocal -> transpiled composeHeightC on glsl-rt) cost ~325us/sample because glsl-rt vec ops (add/sub/mul/mix/vec3/sw) allocate a NEW JS array per op, and the two hot leaf noise fns snoise3/shash3 (~60-70 calls/sample) each did ~60-80 allocs -> ~4-5k short-lived arrays/sample + GC churn. FIX (mapspinner commit, glsl-rt.js + scripts/gen-height.mjs + regenerated src/height-gen.js): hand-write SCALAR snoise3/shash3 in glsl-rt.js (pure-number arithmetic, SAME float ops in SAME order/associativity - mix=a+(b-a)*t, dot=x*x'+y*y'+z*z', same 0.3183099/19.19 hash consts) and teach gen-height.mjs to EMIT CALLS g.snoise3/g.shash3 instead of inlining the transpiled vec bodies (SCALAR_LEAVES set, removed from HEIGHT_FNS, parseCall emits the call). Result ~17x faster (325us->19-37us/sample), BIT-IDENTICAL (golden height-cpu.test.js 12/12 + the git-diff-exit-code regen gate pass). Verify rule: NEVER hand-edit height-gen.js (DO NOT EDIT header + npm test git-diff gate); the change must come from gen-height.mjs regenerating. PROPAGATION (spoint can't npm-publish mapspinner, E401): vendor the 2 runtime files (scripts/mapspinner-perf/glsl-rt.js + gen-height.mjs) + a postinstall scripts/patch-mapspinner.mjs that copies them into node_modules/mapspinner + reruns gen-height.mjs; npm install triggers it so BOTH local dev + gh-pages (which runs npm install) get the fast sampler. Remove the vendor once mapspinner republishes. ALSO this turn: VegPlacement.classify reorder (density coin BEFORE the elevation sample - treelineMul<=1 below the 4000m treeline so a coin>=baseDensity cell rejects with ZERO height samples; same coin re-checked against the faded accept = output-identical) ~27% faster prewarm; RockPlacement density-CEILING reject (rockDensity monotonic in slopeRatio so max at slope=1; coin>=ceiling rejects without the 4 slope samples, re-checked = output-identical); both keep their golden+client/server-parity tests byte-identical. With the fast sampler, the physics heightfield went resolution 4m->2m (N=64->128) and STILL builds faster (2018ms vs 2330ms) for sharper collision. Witness tooling: scripts/{veg-profile,veg-witness,move-witness,gizmo-witness,diag-witness,hf-witness,rock-witness}.mjs are self-contained direct-Playwright probes (no plugkit browser-verb 14s cap). Subagent fan-out (general-purpose Agent) did the transpiler scalarization in mapspinner with 'npm test must pass bit-identical' as the hard gate - worked first try. Supersedes the 'sampler is the keystone, deferred' note in [[height-sampler-perf-shared-heightmap]].